= Biological sequence — Technical =

A sequence can be formalized as s=s₁…sₙ over an alphabet Σ, optionally with ambiguity symbols and associated quality/coordinate metadata. Computational treatment must distinguish raw reads, consensus/assembly sequences, reference sequences, translated sequences, and derived/annotated feature records.

== Modeling / evidence cautions ==
* biological sequence ≠ physical molecule
* sequence ≠ sequence annotation
* sequence similarity ≠ functional identity

